    "result_text": "Done. The build is green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), computed on creation as: start at 1, +1 when an email is present, +1 when `namesakeCount` is 0, capped at 3.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `membershipTier` (string) response property with `membershipLevel` (`integer`, `int32`, min 1 / max 3, `readOnly`), including a description of the derivation. The `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec at build time, so the field name change propagates to the DTO.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 swapped the `membershipTier` mapping (old GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE logic driven by `householdSize`) for a `membershipLevel` expression: `Math.min(3, 1 + emailPresent + namesake0)`.\n\n3. **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel=` (computed with the same rule) instead of nothing tier-related, satisfying \"anything that recorded the tier must record the level instead.\" Verified in the log output: `AUDIT - Owner created id=11 ... membershipLevel=3`.\n\n4. **`AssignHouseholdSize.java`** \u2014 removed the now-stale Javadoc comment referencing the GOLD membership tier (the only consumer of `householdSize`'s tier logic). The `householdSize` field itself is still assigned/stored, just no longer feeds a tier.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` passes: an owner with an email and a unique name (namesakeCount 0) returns `membershipLevel` 3.",
